"Identifier names in this file average about one character, which means it "
"was minified. That is how every production JavaScript build is shipped. It "
"describes how the file was compiled, not anything in it."

msgid "Uses eval()"
msgstr "Uses eval()"

msgid ""
"eval() runs a string as code. Several long-standing libraries use it "
"internally — ExtJS, OpenLayers and MapLibre all do — so it is expected in a "
"bundle that includes them. It is worth attention only if it appears in an "
"app’s own code, or if the string being run could come from user input."
msgstr ""
"eval() runs a string as code. Several long-standing libraries use it "
"internally — ExtJS, OpenLayers and MapLibre all do — so it is expected in a "
"bundle that includes them. It is worth attention only if it appears in an "
"app’s own code, or if the string being run could come from user input."

msgid "References the Function constructor"
msgstr "References the Function constructor"

msgid ""
"Bundled libraries use Function(\"return this\") to locate the global "
"object; lodash and most UMD wrappers contain it. The constructor is "
"reported because it can also turn a string into code, but a fixed string "
"like this one cannot be influenced by an attacker."
msgstr ""
"Bundled libraries use Function(\"return this\") to locate the global "
"object; lodash and most UMD wrappers contain it. The constructor is "
"reported because it can also turn a string into code, but a fixed string "
"like this one cannot be influenced by an attacker."

msgid "Long encoded-looking string"
msgstr "Long encoded-looking string"

msgid ""
"A long run of hex or base64-like characters. In practice these are "
"checksums, file-format signatures, or embedded assets such as icons. It "
"would only matter if the string decoded to code that the app then ran."
msgstr ""
"A long run of hex or base64-like characters. In practice these are "
"checksums, file-format signatures, or embedded assets such as icons. It "
"would only matter if the string decoded to code that the app then ran."

