msgid "Run obfuscation and code analysis"
msgstr "Run obfuscation and code analysis"

msgid ""
"Off by default. Parses each app bundle looking for obfuscation, eval and "
"encoded strings. On minified production code these findings come almost "
"entirely from bundled libraries such as React and lodash, so they are "
"reported as information and never set an app's status. The analysis is also "
"the slowest part of a scan, roughly a second per bundle. Checks for "
"known-vulnerable libraries and for changed app code do not use it and "
"always run. Turn it on to examine an app you have reason to distrust."
msgstr ""
"Off by default. Parses each app bundle looking for obfuscation, eval and "
"encoded strings. On minified production code these findings come almost "
"entirely from bundled libraries such as React and lodash, so they are "
"reported as information and never set an app's status. The analysis is also "
"the slowest part of a scan, roughly a second per bundle. Checks for "
"known-vulnerable libraries and for changed app code do not use it and "
"always run. Turn it on to examine an app you have reason to distrust."

msgid "Maximum Files Scanned Per App"
msgstr "Maximum Files Scanned Per App"

msgid ""
"The Apps Audit follows an app’s module graph (entry scripts, modulepreloads "
"and lazy-loaded chunks). This bounds how many files one app may contribute. "
"DHIS2 2.43 apps use 2-5. Anything skipped because of this limit is listed "
"in the findings."
msgstr ""
"The Apps Audit follows an app’s module graph (entry scripts, modulepreloads "
"and lazy-loaded chunks). This bounds how many files one app may contribute. "
"DHIS2 2.43 apps use 2-5. Anything skipped because of this limit is listed "
"in the findings."

msgid "Maximum MB Scanned Per App"
msgstr "Maximum MB Scanned Per App"

